  "answer_text": "If you are looking for the iconic **Spiegel Home and Fashion Catalog** to shop online, **the company is no longer in business**. \n\nSpiegel officially ceased all operations and quietly took down its shopping website (`spiegel.com`) in **2019** after struggling to transition from its historic mail-order print format to the digital era. \n\nHowever, depending on what you are looking for, you can find vintage catalogs or shop at excellent modern alternatives that match Spiegel\u2019s classic style.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Where to Find Vintage Spiegel Catalogs\nIf you are feeling nostalgic or seeking vintage interior design and fashion inspiration from the mid-to-late 20th century, you can still buy physical retro Spiegel Catalogs:\n* **eBay & Etsy:** Private collectors frequently sell vintage Spiegel Home and Fashion catalogs from the 1950s, '60s, '70s, '80s, and '90s. These are highly sought after by retro lovers and collectors.\n* **The Internet Archive:** You can view scanned, digital pages of old retail catalogs, including Spiegel, for free on Archive.org.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Best Alternative Online Home Decor Catalogs\nIf you loved the elegant bedding, furniture, and unique accents of the Spiegel Home catalog, several direct-mail and online catalog brands offer a similar aesthetic today:\n\n* **Touch of Class** (`touchofclass.com`): Known for its high-quality, elegant, and classic home furnishings. They specialize in detailed bedding, comforter sets, area rugs, and distinctive home art.\n* **Country Door** (`countrydoor.com`): Offers beautiful rustic, modern-farmhouse, and cozy home decor. Like many classic catalog companies, they also offer a \"buy now, pay later\" credit program.\n* **Grandin Road** (`grandinroad.com`): Focuses on bright, sophisticated, and designer-inspired indoor and outdoor home decor, seasonal updates, and unique furniture pieces.\n* **The Lakeside Collection** (`lakeside.com`): If you liked Spiegel\u2019s more budget-friendly home accessories and organizational tools, Lakeside offers highly affordable household items, gifts, and seasonal decorations.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Best Alternative Fashion Catalogs\nIf you are missing Spiegel's sophisticated, career-focused, and trend-right women's apparel:\n* **Boston Proper** (`bostonproper.com`): Offers high-quality, bold, and upscale women's fashion that very closely mirrors the \"chic, confident woman\" aesthetic that Spiegel championed in the '80s and '90s.\n* **ModCloth** (`modcloth.com`): Great for finding vintage-inspired, retro, and feminine dress styles.",
